{% block subheader %}
<p class="intro">This page outlines my work in ethnography and creative practice, spanning anthropology, science and technology studies (STS), multimodal inventions, and urban research, all unified by a focus on fragments—tiny traces that reflect everyday life's hidden complexity. For me, ethnography is more than description; it's a curatorial and experimental process that uses fieldnotes, illustrations, and other devices to capture, document, and reimagine possible worlds. My research is both analytical and imaginative. My ethnographic focus is on understanding life in fragmented, more-than-human realms through residues, urban infrastructure, multispecies encounters, and speculative archives.</p>
{% endblock %}

